  "published": "2026-08-19T21:49:49.5Z",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.2.0 — NEW: CasperCloudX402Client, a client for the CSPR.cloud x402 Facilitator API (https://x402-facilitator.cspr.cloud): GetSupportedAsync, VerifyAsync and SettleAsync over the x402 v2 protocol with the Casper \"exact\" scheme (CEP-3009 transfer_with_authorization signed authorizations). Ships the full protocol object model under CSPR.Cloud.Net.Objects.X402 (PaymentRequired challenge, PaymentPayload with the Casper authorization/publicKey/signature payload, facilitator request/response types). Amounts are strings end-to-end; protocol JSON is camelCase; every method takes a trailing optional CancellationToken. Note the facilitator answers HTTP 200 even for a failed settlement — branch on X402SettleResponse.Success, never the status code. Purely additive: no changes to existing REST or streaming APIs. Earlier: v4.1.0 added CancellationToken to every REST method; v4.0.x made money values decimal and added opt-in per-row tolerance with SkippedItemCount.",
